      'Eddard Stark was the second son of Rickard Stark, raised to rule only after the Mad King roasted his father and strangled his brother Brandon. He rode south with Robert Baratheon in the rebellion that followed, took the sack of King’s Landing as a wound rather than a victory, and came home with a sister’s bones and a bastard he would not explain. For fifteen years he kept the North by the old laws: a man who passes the sentence swings the sword, guests eat salt, and a promise to Lyanna is kept even when it poisons his marriage.\n\nRobert’s visit to Winterfell ends that peace. Ned is named Hand, dragged into a capital that runs on whispers, and asked to pretend that Joffrey, Myrcella, and Tommen are Robert’s blood. He is a great lord and a poor player. He will not seize children in the night, will not buy the City Watch until it is too late, and will not take Littlefinger’s offered knife. Honor is the only armor he trusts, and in King’s Landing it is made of paper.',
