      'Robb Stark was Ned’s heir, raised on winter and honor, old enough to rule a castle and too young to rule a war. When his father is taken, he calls the northern banners as a boy-lord and wins like a man who has been waiting his whole life to prove the blood. Grey Wind runs beside him. The Whispering Wood makes him a legend. His bannermen name him King in the North rather than bend to Joffrey or to Stannis or to Renly.\n\nHe is a brilliant field commander and a disastrous politician. He will not trade Jaime for a peace he thinks is slavery. He sends Theon home because he still believes in fostering. He marries Talisa for love after promising a Frey daughter for a bridge. Every victory in the field makes the next betrayal in a hall more certain.',
