    backstory:
      'Sansa Stark was raised on songs: knights, tourneys, a queen in a golden crown. She is Ned and Catelyn’s eldest daughter, trained for a southern marriage, and she wants that life so badly she will betray her own sister to keep it. Joffrey Baratheon is the prince in the song until he is not. What follows is an education no septa prepared her for — Cersei’s smiles, Littlefinger’s lessons, Ramsay’s hunt, and the long work of turning courtesy into a weapon.\n\nBy the end she is not a little bird. She is the one Stark who learned the game in the places it is actually played, then took that knowledge home and used it to keep the North. She does not want the Iron Throne. She wants Winterfell, and she will not give it to a dragon queen or to a brother who kneels.',
