      2: 'Season 2 Arya is a prisoner who refuses to be one. Yoren’s band is smashed. She is marched to Harrenhal, where she serves Tywin Lannister wine and listens harder than any lord in the room. Jaqen H’ghar owes her three deaths and she spends them like a girl who has learned that names are knives. She leaves Harrenhal with Gendry and Hot Pie, the coin for Braavos in her pocket, and a colder understanding of what she is becoming.',
      3: 'Season 3 Arya falls in with the Brotherhood Without Banners, is sold to the Hound, and is dragged toward the Twins just in time to see her family butchered through the rain. She cannot save Robb. She cannot save her mother. She kills a Frey in the mud afterward because the list is the only law she has left. The girl who wanted to be a knight is gone. The girl who will settle accounts is not.',
      4: 'Season 4 Arya travels with Sandor Clegane, a killer who is also the closest thing she has to a protector. They take a farmer’s silver, they fight, they almost reach the Eyrie too late for Lysa. The Hound is wounded in a fight with Brienne and Arya leaves him to die rather than give him the gift of mercy. She finds a Braavosi ship, speaks Valar Morghulis, and sails east toward the House of Black and White.',
      5: 'Season 5 Arya is a novice of the Many-Faced God. She buries Needle under a rock, then cannot quite become no one. Jaqen and the Waif teach her to see without eyes, to lie, to kill on assignment. She takes a face and kills Ser Meryn Trant for herself instead of for the god. The House punishes her with blindness. She is still Arya Stark, and that is both her failure and her strength.',
      6: 'Season 6 Arya wins her sight back the hard way, fights the Waif through the streets of Braavos, and takes the girl’s face as proof that she can be no one — and then chooses to be Arya anyway. She retrieves Needle, sails home, and stops at the Twins. Walder Frey drinks a toast poured by a serving girl who is his own dead daughter’s face. House Frey ends at supper. Arya is coming north.',
      7: 'Season 7 Arya returns to Winterfell as a stranger her own sister cannot read. She is a trained assassin in a pack of surviving Starks, suspicious of Sansa, watched by Littlefinger, and still the girl who once sewed a direwolf banner in this hall. With Bran’s sight she turns Littlefinger’s game inside out. Her dagger takes him under the heart tree. The list has one less name, and the pack is together.',
      8: 'Season 8 Arya is the weapon the living did not know they had. Melisandre reminds her that brown eyes, blue eyes, and green eyes are all the same to Death. In the godswood she leaps onto the Night King and drives the Valyrian catspaw into him; the dead fall with their maker. After the fire of King’s Landing she is done with lists. She will not stay for a throne or a marriage. She takes a ship west of Westeros, toward maps that still have blank edges.',
