      'Jon Snow grows up in Winterfell’s halls and not quite in its family: Ned’s bastard, Catelyn’s wound, the brothers’ shadow. He takes the black because the Night’s Watch is the one honor a bastard can claim without asking anyone for a name. At the Wall he finds brothers, a direwolf called Ghost, and a war older than the thrones in the south.\n\nHe is Ned’s son in every way that matters and Rhaegar’s in the ways that will wreck a queen. He kneels, he rises, he dies, he comes back, he loves Daenerys Targaryen, and he still puts a knife in her because the man raised by Ned Stark cannot watch the world burn for a crown he never wanted. The North sends him beyond the Wall again. It is the only ending that fits.',
