      2: 'Season 2 Jon ranges north with Qhorin Halfhand, kills a brother to prove himself to the wildlings, and falls into Ygritte’s orbit. He is a crow among free folk, lying for the Watch and meaning some of the lies. The Wall is far. The boy who took the black is learning that oaths and people do not always fit in the same hand.',
      3: 'Season 3 Jon loves Ygritte and still belongs to the Watch. He climbs the Wall with the free folk, cannot fire on the boys in Castle Black, and chooses his brothers when the moment comes. Ygritte’s arrows find him. He lives. The Battle of Castle Black is still ahead, but Jon Snow has already picked a side, and it is not the side that kisses him in the cave.',
      4: 'Season 4 Jon holds the Wall. He leads the defense of Castle Black against Magnar Styr and Tormund, kills the Thenn, and watches Ygritte die in the yard. Stannis arrives in time to smash Mance’s host. Jon executes Janos Slynt, is elected Lord Commander, and inherits a brotherhood that hates the choice he is about to make: the wildlings must come south, or they will come as wights.',
      5: 'Season 5 Jon treats with Mance, then watches Stannis burn him. He sails to Hardhome, sees the Night King raise the dead, and brings as many free folk through the Wall as will come. Castle Black calls it treason. Olly and the mutineers stab him in the snow under the words For the Watch. Jon Snow dies in the dark, a Lord Commander murdered by his own men.',
      6: 'Season 6 Melisandre puts the red god to work and Jon gasps back into a life he does not want. He hangs the mutineers, gives the Watch to Edd, and rides south as a son of Winterfell again. Ramsay has Rickon. The Battle of the Bastards nearly buries Jon in a crush of his own dead until Sansa’s Vale knights break the line. The northern lords name him King in the North. Ghost stands beside a crown Jon never asked for.',
      7: 'Season 7 Jon goes to Dragonstone to ask a Targaryen for help against the dead and finds a queen, a dragon, and a love that complicates every vow. He kneels to Daenerys to get her north. He leads the wight hunt, is saved by Drogon and a uncle’s last ride, and shows Cersei a corpse that still does not buy a real alliance. Sam and Bran give him the rest: he is Aegon Targaryen, trueborn. He does not want that either.',
      8: 'Season 8 Jon fights the Long Night in the yard at Winterfell, loves Daenerys, and watches her burn King’s Landing after the bells. He tells her she is his queen. He tells her he cannot forget the ash. In the throne room he kisses her and puts a dagger in her heart. Grey Worm wants his head. Tyrion bargains an exile. Jon Snow rides north of the Wall with Ghost and the free folk, a king who would rather be a crow again.',
