    aliases: ['Dany', 'Khaleesi', 'Mother of Dragons', 'Breaker of Chains', 'The Unburnt', 'Mhysa'],
    backstory:
      'Daenerys Targaryen is born on Dragonstone as her family dies in King’s Landing, then raised in exile on the kindness of strangers and the cruelty of her brother Viserys. She is sold to Khal Drogo for an army she does not want, finds a spine in the grass sea, and walks into a funeral pyre with three stone eggs. She walks out unburnt, a mother of dragons, and the last Targaryen who still thinks the Iron Throne is a birthright and a rescue.\n\nShe learns to rule in Slaver’s Bay the hard way: cities freed, cities restless, advisors who love her and advisors who use her. She comes west as a liberator with a northern king at her side. She ends as the Mad King’s daughter in the snow of ash, certain that mercy is how her family dies. Jon’s knife is the last kindness anyone shows her.',
    accomplishments: [
      'Hatched three dragons in Drogo’s pyre and survived the fire unburnt',
      'Sacked Astapor, broke Yunkai’s slave host, and took Meereen as queen',
      'Survived the fighting pits, Daznak’s trap, and a Dothraki capture, then flew Drogon out of Vaes Dothrak',
      'Brought dragons, Dothraki, and Unsullied to Westeros and took the war to Cersei',
      'Destroyed the Iron Fleet and, after the bells, burned King’s Landing',
    ],
    score: 90,
    scoreWhy:
      'The most powerful living Targaryen of the age — breaker of chains, mother of dragons, and finally the queen who would rather burn a city than share it.',
    seasons: {
      1: 'Season 1 Daenerys is a frightened girl in a Pentoshi manse, translated and sold. Viserys trades her to Drogo; she learns Dothraki, learns her own body, and learns that she can stop a khalasar with a word if she is willing to be a queen instead of a sister. Drogo dies in a blood magic tent. She walks into his pyre with the eggs. Dawn gives her three hatchlings and a name the grass sea will not forget: Mother of Dragons.',
      2: 'Season 2 Daenerys is a khaleesi without a khalasar, starving toward Qarth. The House of the Undying shows her thrones and snow and a Blue Heart that wants her small. She takes her dragons back from Pyat Pree, refuses to stay a curiosity in a merchant city, and turns toward the slave coasts with a handful of bloodriders and a stolen future.',
      3: 'Season 3 Daenerys becomes a conqueror. In Astapor she bargains for the Unsullied, then sacks the Wise Masters with a word: dracarys. Yunkai falls to Grey Worm, Jorah, and Daario. She is Mhysa in the streets, a breaker of chains who has not yet learned what comes after the breaking. Jorah’s love and Barristan’s honesty start to pull her toward Westeros. Slaver’s Bay is not done with her.',
      4: 'Season 4 Daenerys takes Meereen, nails slavemasters to miles, and sits a harpy’s throne because she will not sail west and leave a vacuum of cruelty behind her. She chains two dragons after they kill a child. She rules, slowly and badly, a city that does not want a foreign savior. The Breaker of Chains discovers that ruling is a different art from freeing.',
      5: 'Season 5 Daenerys tries to be a queen of compromise: Hizdahr, the pits, a marriage to still the Sons of the Harpy. It is a trap. The fighting pit explodes in knives; Drogon answers; she flies, for the first time, as a dragonrider. She lands among a Dothraki horde that sees only a stray khaleesi. The girl from Pentos is gone. The woman on the dragon is not yet willing to burn everything.',
      6: 'Season 6 Daenerys burns the khals in Vaes Dothrak and walks out of the temple as the Unburnt a second time. She unchains her dragons, appoints Tyrion to run Meereen, and finally turns the fleet toward Westeros. The promise of her childhood — the Iron Throne, the House of the Dragon — is no longer a story Viserys told. It is a course heading.',
      7: 'Season 7 Daenerys lands on Dragonstone, the island of her birth, with the largest host in the living world. She takes the Reach and the Rock by fire and blood, loses a dragon to the Night King on a frozen lake, and falls in love with Jon Snow. She agrees to fight the dead before the lion. It is the most generous thing she does in Westeros, and it costs her Viserion.',
      8: 'Season 8 Daenerys wins the Long Night and loses the North’s love. Missandei dies. Rhaegal dies. Jon’s true name makes her claim a story she cannot control. When the bells of King’s Landing ring she burns the city anyway, standing on Drogon as the Red Keep comes down on Cersei. She talks of breaking the world’s wheel. Jon kills her in the throne room. Drogon melts the Iron Throne and carries her body east. The Mother of Dragons does not get a grave in Westeros.',
    },
