    backstory:
      'Stannis Baratheon is Robert’s middle brother, the one who held Storm’s End through a siege on rats and onions, the one who took Dragonstone because he was told to, the one who never got the thanks he thought duty was owed. He is rigid, just, and starved for a love the world will not give him. Melisandre tells him he is Azor Ahai, and he wants it to be true because it would mean the thankless years were a prophecy instead of a slight.\n\nHe is the rightful king by the law Ned died for. He is also the man who burns his own daughter in the snow when the ice will not melt. The North does not take him. Brienne’s sword does.',
